<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:36:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Mladic's death, Bosnia and Serbia's unfinished reckoning</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eca652077849b86bc795773946c7591f435b73bd830f3cb0e094be1d584f831b</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733--19ecd75a4666.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mladic-s-death-bosnia-and-serbia-s-unfinished-reckoning/a-78602733?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Ratko Mladic did not close a dark chapter of European history; it reopened old wounds. The ideology that created him lives on. The Dayton Peace Agreement ended the war, not the divisions that produced it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will Bangladesh join the Mecca defense pact?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e11c8995e83716a5558e65e9a097754829981785a955e19464197b6bd973e298</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-pact/a-78613944--2a3eb0616221.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-pact/a-78613944?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Bangladesh is weighing the risks of joining the Mecca mutual defense alliance, experts warn that any move to join the pact could complicate relations with neighboring India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Norway's new King Haakon VIII takes oath in parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd3b2548684ba8b71e6456c85da872fdff4d0ffcaea64d6385a0cc040459e22a</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:35:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923--1723f25a617f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-s-new-king-haakon-viii-takes-oath-in-parliament/a-78606923?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new king swore to uphold the constitution in parliament in Oslo, the first major institutional step of his reign. Haakon VIII's wife Queen Mette-Marit had to skip the event in the aftermath of her lung transplant.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood: Death toll tops 1,000 as rescue continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:596874391b62e9b9407355499cceefd910759fa7156378d9065fa5936b7875bd</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:36:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460--79d1a5a29fe8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepalese authorities say 4,000 people remain unaccounted for as rescue teams with search dogs comb through mud, rocks and debris.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US irks Germany, Europe with Russian G20 invite, press bans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fc29d15f74b4486e4e5ab6baaccecb00cec81ac1209e7348be954ca0ddf82ce</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:36:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919--0e3658fe72cb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-irks-germany-europe-with-russian-g20-invite-press-bans/a-78583919?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's finance minister is at the G20 meeting in Asheville but some key US press corps members are not. The mood was already tense amid the lengthy Iran war and Trump's renewed beef with neighbor Canada.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can new Apple CEO John Ternus fix the tech giant's AI woes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a22618bcb3c8d47166b7a0ee2622ed130d17a72b99e33f59aa76a6a8bf4c8ee</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:36:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898--3dbcd845fd90.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">John Ternus is just the third Apple CEO in 30 years. His primary challenge is to correct the company's faltering AI strategy to preserve its position as a big tech leader.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Lionel Messi announces retirement from international football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5fcd70e766fd23ca7cb84df38a19010cedf2d6af5589c53e20a239f994bc36e</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:36:11Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lionel-messi-announces-retirement-from-international-football/a-78579502--40b32b537f9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lionel-messi-announces-retirement-from-international-football/a-78579502?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Argentine legend announced that he will not play for the national team again, ending an illustrious international career.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How China buried Tibet flood images after Nepal disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38aded01db10c4ad1cab2dfad25edfac79dd398b88db8055f68c3a8cfdb4dae3</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:40Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-china-buried-tibet-flood-images-after-nepal-disaster/a-78576472--f156a9510413.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-china-buried-tibet-flood-images-after-nepal-disaster/a-78576472?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In Tibet, a digital crackdown followed the deadly flood that has devastated communities along the China-Nepal border. Censors erased viral footage while Chinese state media flooded platforms with official content.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Deceived and deployed: How young Cameroonians end up fighting in Russia's war in Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d9ebf41301ac6978d4797f91290ebefb2a97abb76f718eca22ce63e310e2666</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:40Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deceived-and-deployed-how-young-cameroonians-end-up-fighting-in-russia-s-war-in-ukraine/a-78513256--672bb0ec1fd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deceived-and-deployed-how-young-cameroonians-end-up-fighting-in-russia-s-war-in-ukraine/a-78513256?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts say economic desperation and fraudulent recruitment schemes are funneling Cameroonian youth into the Russian military — with deadly consequences.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tariffs spat: Carney bets Canada can defy Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a33f521e9a148e2fb2fd161b336279d4ad352eb884e4282cb535f50f0342bd3</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:40Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tariffs-spat-carney-bets-canada-can-defy-trump/a-78542754--cb80db02622b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tariffs-spat-carney-bets-canada-can-defy-trump/a-78542754?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada is facing new US import penalties after Prime Minister Mark Carney refused to match US tariffs on China. Other countries are watching as the Trump trade clash turns into a fight over economic sovereignty.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Putin-Modi meeting at SCO: Can Russia-India ties hold?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:88b053d17f3272f29e38e01558d77c0816e4e56500b3a6b8b59e8d18481a97e7</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:40Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/putin-modi-meeting-at-sco-can-russia-india-ties-hold/a-78575121--4d39471eea4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/putin-modi-meeting-at-sco-can-russia-india-ties-hold/a-78575121?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian Prime Minister Modi and Russian President Putin are at the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation (SCO) summit in Kyrgyzstan as Moscow and New Delhi face rising tensions with Washington.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal floods test PM Balen's young government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f8ef4478414c117d2dda67c21b44de0bbab784076f02cd7f0d3920989f33ff2</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:40Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T11:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-floods-test-pm-balen-s-young-government/a-78574227--fd76d80623d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-floods-test-pm-balen-s-young-government/a-78574227?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A year after Gen Z-led protests swept Prime Minister Balendra "Balen" Shah to power, deadly floods are testing his government's ability to manage a national crisis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Niger's failed coup exposes cracks in the military — and Russia's influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08caca646547287fc910b073876a66c846d34af731ce2020c91a51592de73041</id><updated>2026-09-01T13:33:40Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T11:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/niger-s-failed-coup-exposes-cracks-in-the-military-and-russia-s-influence/a-78572278--256c8fdbe25e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/niger-s-failed-coup-exposes-cracks-in-the-military-and-russia-s-influence/a-78572278?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The failed coup in Niger has brought deep divisions within the military to light. As Russia's support highlights the junta's fading influence, soldiers continue to face jihadi attacks, poor equipment and little pay.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
